
Save your synthetic or real observations into a csv file and place in run/observations directory.

The csv file should contain the following column headers:

'azimuth', 'date', 'days', 'elevation', 'error_var', 'height', 'index', 'kind', 'lat', 'lon', 'seconds', 'utime', 'value', 'x', 'y', 'z'

VARIABLE DESCRIPTIONS

date        -  full date, can use datetime object or Timestamp
days        -  days since 1601-01-01 00:00:00
utime       -  seconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00
seconds     -  seconds since start of current day

x           -  meters. x location relative to radar
y           -  meters. y location relative to radar
z           -  meters. height relative to radar
lat         -  deg latitude (relative to assigned lat0/lon0 for radar location in namelist.py)
lon         -  deg longitude (relative to assigned lat0/lon0 for radar location in namelist.py)
elevation   -  deg. elevation angle of radar data
azimuth     -  deg. Zero is north. azimuth of radar data
value       -  data value 

kind        -  observation type: 11 = VR, 12 = DBZ, 13 = DBZ0, 14=DBZ0_W (see namelist readme for info on what these variables are)
error_var   -  observation error variance (error squared). This is overwritten in computeHx.py using error values assigned in namelist 
index       -  rangeIndex for data (0 to N observations)
